│ Reasoning: The issue lies in concurrent invocations on the same    │
│ Agent instance corrupting the internal state since no concurrency  │
│ control is applied. The fix involves:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Initializing an asyncio.Lock in the Agent constructor to        │
│    protect invocation concurrency.                                 │
│  2 Wrapping the top-level async invocation method invoke_async     │
│    with an async lock acquisition.                                 │
│  3 If the lock is already held (another invocation ongoing), a     │
│    concurrency exception should be raised to prevent parallel      │
│    execution.                                                      │
│  4 Modifying the synchronous __call__ method is optional because   │
│    it just calls invoke_async via run_async, but it is good        │
│    practice to propagate concurrency exceptions properly.          │
│                                                                    │
│ The following changes will be done:                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • In __init__, add self._invocation_lock = asyncio.Lock()         │
│  • Define a new concurrency exception (e.g.,                       │
│    AgentConcurrentInvocationException) in the module (assuming     │
│    it's suitable to add near the Agent class, or could reuse an    │
│    existing exception if available — here we'll define it).        │
│  • In invoke_async, attempt to acquire the lock without waiting    │
│    (lock.acquire with timeout=0 is not standard asyncio, but       │
│    instead we use lock.acquire() along with lock.locked() to check │
│    if concurrent). Since asyncio.Lock doesn't support timeout or   │
│    try_acquire, we can:                                            │
│     • check if locked and raise concurrency exception              │
│     • else acquire the lock and run the invocation, releasing      │
│       afterward.                                                   │
│  • The concurrency exception will be raised immediately on         │
│    concurrent attempt.                                             │
│                                                                    │
