│                                                                    │
│ The issue is about parallel invocations on the same Agent instance │
│ corrupting the internal state. To fix this, we should ensure that  │
│ only one invocation can run at a time on an Agent instance.        │
│                                                                    │
│ We can use an asyncio lock to block concurrent asynchronous        │
│ invocations. If a concurrent call is attempted, instead of         │
│ waiting, we raise a concurrency exception immediately.             │
│                                                                    │
│ Changes to implement:                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  1 In the Agent.__init__ method, initialize an asyncio.Lock named, │
│    for example, _invocation_lock.                                  │
│  2 Modify the asynchronous method invoke_async to acquire the lock │
│    in a non-blocking manner at the start of the method. If the     │
│    lock is already held (meaning the agent is busy), raise a       │
│    concurrency exception immediately.                              │
│  3 Make sure the lock is released after invocation finishes,       │
│    whether successfully or by exception.                           │
│  4 Define a new exception class, InvocationConcurrencyError, for   │
│    this concurrency failure.                                       │
│  5 Modify the synchronous call __call__ so that when it calls      │
│    invoke_async it properly propagates this concurrency exception  │
│    to the caller.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ This approach ensures that any simultaneous invocation attempt on  │
│ the same agent will fail fast, protecting the internal state.      │
