│ This continuation of the stream_async method shows that it resumes │
│ the interrupt state and resets usage metrics at the start. Then it │
│ merges invocation_state and any deprecated kwargs into a single    │
│ state dictionary. It retrieves the callback handler to be used and │
│ converts the input prompt to a list of messages asynchronously. It │
│ starts a tracing span for telemetry and enters a try block where   │
│ it runs the asynchronous event loop (_run_loop), which yields      │
│ events asynchronously. For each yielded event, it prepares it with │
│ invocation state, calls the callback handler if the event is a     │
│ callback event, and yields the event dictionary. After event loop  │
│ completion, it creates an AgentResult from the last event's stop   │
│ information, calls the callback handler with the result, yields an │
│ AgentResultEvent, and ends the trace span. Exceptions during the   │
